WEBVTT

00:43:59.085 --> 00:44:01.473
it's not the death I would
want you to have,

00:44:01.497 --> 00:44:04.111
it's not the death that I tried
to orchestrate for her,

00:44:04.135 --> 00:44:07.973
but it's a death that was absolutely
in keeping with who she was.

00:44:07.997 --> 00:44:11.498
And I've kind of got to hand it to her
for staying consistent to the theme

00:44:11.522 --> 00:44:14.303
for the entire life,

00:44:14.327 --> 00:44:18.583
of going through life
with her fists up and just being epic.

00:44:18.607 --> 00:44:20.790
That was who she was.

00:44:20.814 --> 00:44:24.265
CA: Is there anything else you'd share
with people about grief?

00:44:24.289 --> 00:44:26.080
I mean, it's one of these topics

00:44:26.104 --> 00:44:30.140
that isn't comfortably talked about
that much by many people.